      "side": 1,
      "message": "A couple of issues with backward-reference mirroring at `layer_depth \u003c\u003d 1`:\n\n1. At `layer_depth \u003d\u003d 1`, it looks like backward references are skipped by `skip_ref_for_layer_depth()` in all subsequent stages (`pyramid_me_level2`/`level1`/`level0`, `prepare_best_pme_stats`, `post_pyramid_me`), so mirroring `pre_pme_stats` at `layer_depth \u003d\u003d 1` may be unused work. (I could be wrong here).  that can abort encoding via `aom_internal_error` if no symmetric `-rel_dist` forward reference is present in `ref_disp_order_idx`.\n2. Negating `mv` on lines 1122-1123 without clamping can put `(x_search_center, y_search_center)` outside the `-64` border in `post_pyramid_me()` line 1473 (which indexes `ref_y-\u003ebuf` before `clamp_search_area()` at line 1485) when `last_pyr_level \u003d\u003d PYR_LEVEL2`.\n3. Consider avoiding `aom_internal_error` here - it looks like we should use an assert instead maybe?",
